WEBVTT

00:17.184 --> 00:21.272
- [Boyd] Previously on From...
- Come here. Come here.

00:21.355 --> 00:23.315
Oh, no!

00:23.399 --> 00:24.692
[sobbing hysterically]

00:25.860 --> 00:27.737
"Knowledge comes at a cost"?

00:27.820 --> 00:29.447
It killed Jim because of us.

00:29.530 --> 00:30.614
"Anghkooey."

00:30.698 --> 00:32.533
It means "remember."

00:32.616 --> 00:35.035
[Boyd] These kids keep
calling you back to help them.

00:35.119 --> 00:37.496
- How do we do it?
- I'm working on it.

00:37.580 --> 00:39.415
[Tabitha] Julie and Ethan.

00:39.498 --> 00:41.333
I don't know how,
but I'm gonna find a way

00:41.417 --> 00:43.836
to take care of them,
to keep them safe.

00:43.919 --> 00:45.463
- I don't wanna be here anymore!
- Ethan!

00:45.546 --> 00:47.673
What did you do?
Why didn't he come home?

00:47.757 --> 00:49.842
- I did nothing.
- You're lying!

00:49.925 --> 00:51.469
I want Dad!

00:51.552 --> 00:52.720
[Jim] Ethan.

00:54.680 --> 00:58.184
The night we arrived here,
you had a dream.

00:58.267 --> 00:59.935
- Lake of Tears?
- It's here.

01:00.019 --> 01:01.896
And I need you to find it.

01:01.979 --> 01:03.981
Ethan called it
"Storywalking."

01:04.064 --> 01:06.984
I need you to give me some time,
even if it looks bad.

01:11.530 --> 01:12.406
Dad!

01:14.074 --> 01:15.159
Randall!

01:15.242 --> 01:16.285
[Randall] I got you.

01:16.368 --> 01:17.495
[gasping]

01:17.578 --> 01:19.205
Look at me. Look at me.

01:19.288 --> 01:23.125
[Sophia] Lord, please protect us
in this dark place.

01:23.209 --> 01:24.960
Please stand
by my daddy's bedside

01:25.044 --> 01:27.463
and let him wake
renewed in Your love.

01:27.546 --> 01:28.464
[choking]

01:28.547 --> 01:30.257
My father died.

01:30.341 --> 01:33.135
[Kenny] I'll talk to Boyd
about a burial.

01:33.219 --> 01:34.845
If people find out
what you did...

01:34.929 --> 01:37.389
Help! No!

01:37.473 --> 01:39.475
...that's the kind of thing that
could tear this place apart.

01:39.558 --> 01:41.560
You're gonna tell them
that you lost your eye

01:41.644 --> 01:42.978
trying to help Fatima.

01:43.062 --> 01:44.730
Hey! Hey! Whoa!

01:46.649 --> 01:49.401
I'm a good person
and I don't deserve to be here.

01:49.485 --> 01:50.903
Get the strip.

01:52.029 --> 01:54.365
- What I'm doing is getting out.
- There is no way out!

01:57.618 --> 01:59.829
What the fuck
is wrong with you?

01:59.912 --> 02:02.540
I gave...birth to one of them.

02:02.623 --> 02:04.542
Dad, tell her that's not
what you're saying.

02:04.625 --> 02:06.335
It's the one I killed.

02:06.418 --> 02:11.048
I told all of you that there
was something inside me.

02:23.894 --> 02:25.688
Sorry.

02:25.771 --> 02:27.523
Oh, it's okay.
I'll get out of your way.

02:27.606 --> 02:30.484
No, you don't--

02:30.568 --> 02:32.069
you don't--
you don't need to go.

02:32.152 --> 02:34.154
I just came to get
a glass of water.

02:40.452 --> 02:42.329
Boyd said if people
find out what happened--

02:42.413 --> 02:44.373
I know.

02:44.456 --> 02:47.001
We should probably get
our story straight.

02:58.053 --> 03:00.180
Are you okay?

03:02.433 --> 03:04.852
I'm not really sure
I deserve to be.

03:13.152 --> 03:15.988
Elgin,
I don't want to hate you.

03:16.989 --> 03:20.951
This place took advantage
of both of us.

03:22.661 --> 03:26.206
Neither of us will
ever be the same again.

03:26.290 --> 03:27.333
Will we?

03:27.416 --> 03:30.085
No, we won't.

03:35.674 --> 03:37.635
There's something
I need your help with.

03:49.855 --> 03:52.107
- [gun firing]
- [townspeople screaming]

03:52.191 --> 03:54.193
- [screaming]
- [gun firing]

03:54.276 --> 03:55.986
[Boyd] Abby! Stop!

03:56.070 --> 03:58.322
- [gun cocking]
- No, no!

03:58.405 --> 03:59.490
[gasps]

04:03.577 --> 04:04.954
Oh.

04:05.037 --> 04:06.747
[groans]

04:07.998 --> 04:11.919
Oh, shit. [groans]

04:19.259 --> 04:21.345
You wanna tell me what
the hell that was yesterday?

04:23.764 --> 04:25.265
Not really.

04:25.349 --> 04:27.643
You're gonna have to do
a little better than that.

04:29.061 --> 04:30.562
What do you want me to say?

04:30.646 --> 04:32.481
I want you to tell me

04:32.564 --> 04:34.441
that you're not gonna
lose your shit again

04:34.525 --> 04:36.777
and put people's
lives in danger.

04:36.860 --> 04:39.947
You got lucky yesterday.
You understand that?

04:40.030 --> 04:43.409
If Kristi had gotten hurt,
you and me

04:43.492 --> 04:45.202
are having a different
conversation right now.

04:45.285 --> 04:46.537
Look, whoever
that was yesterday,

04:46.620 --> 04:49.039
that wasn't me, all right?

04:49.123 --> 04:50.666
[sighs]
I don't even wanna be here.

04:50.749 --> 04:52.584
Well, good.
We're working on that.

04:56.630 --> 04:58.799
[exhales heavily]
You know,

04:58.882 --> 05:01.218
Kristi told me yesterday that
she'd seen dozens of people

05:01.301 --> 05:03.595
with dozens of schemes
about how to leave this place.

05:05.222 --> 05:07.266
There's only thing
that they have in common.

05:07.349 --> 05:10.060
You know what it is?

05:10.144 --> 05:11.311
They all died.

05:13.439 --> 05:14.314
Yeah.

05:15.816 --> 05:17.026
Well...

05:18.902 --> 05:20.904
Well, this time
feels different.

05:20.988 --> 05:24.616
Yeah. That's probably
what they thought.

05:24.700 --> 05:27.161
Can you give me a bullet?

05:27.244 --> 05:29.830
I only... need one.

05:30.789 --> 05:32.875
I'll go into the woods,
and look,

05:32.958 --> 05:34.918
don't worry, you won't even
have to clean it up.

05:54.563 --> 05:55.731
Sophia?

05:56.857 --> 05:59.318
I brought you some things
from your dad's car.

05:59.401 --> 06:01.653
Thank you.

06:02.488 --> 06:05.616
We're gonna take him down
to the service now.

06:06.700 --> 06:09.161
Can I have a minute
to say goodbye?

06:09.244 --> 06:10.829
Yeah, of course.

06:10.913 --> 06:12.664
We'll be right outside
when you're ready, okay?

06:12.748 --> 06:14.374
[Sophia] Okay.

06:28.972 --> 06:33.560
[ominous music playing]

06:48.450 --> 06:50.202
You were fun.

06:54.915 --> 06:58.168
I couldn't let you go without
something to remember you by.

07:01.004 --> 07:04.383
[ominous music playing]

07:04.466 --> 07:09.304
[flesh squishing]

07:10.889 --> 07:11.807
[snaps]

07:22.693 --> 07:26.572
["Que Sera, Sera (Whatever Will
Be, Will Be)" plays]

07:32.703 --> 07:37.499
♪ When I was just a little boy ♪

07:37.583 --> 07:39.918
♪ I asked my father ♪

07:40.002 --> 07:42.129
♪ "What will I be?" ♪

07:43.714 --> 07:46.008
♪ "Will I be handsome?" ♪

07:46.091 --> 07:48.510
♪ "Will I be rich?" ♪

07:48.594 --> 07:52.389
♪ Here's what he said to me ♪

07:52.472 --> 07:55.934
♪ Que sera sera ♪

07:56.643 --> 08:01.481
♪ Whatever will be will be ♪

08:01.565 --> 08:05.736
♪ The future's not ours to see ♪

08:05.819 --> 08:08.405
♪ Que sera sera ♪

08:10.866 --> 08:13.827
♪ What will be will be ♪

08:23.253 --> 08:28.050
♪ Now I have
children of my own ♪

08:28.133 --> 08:30.469
♪ They ask their father ♪

08:30.552 --> 08:34.139
♪ "What will I be?" ♪

08:34.223 --> 08:36.683
♪ "Will I be pretty?" ♪

08:36.767 --> 08:39.061
♪ "Will I be rich?" ♪

08:39.144 --> 08:42.940
♪ I tell them tenderly ♪

08:43.023 --> 08:46.526
♪ Que sera sera ♪

08:47.152 --> 08:51.365
♪ Whatever will be will be ♪

08:52.157 --> 08:56.203
♪ The future's not ours to see ♪

08:56.286 --> 08:59.623
♪ Que sera sera ♪

09:01.416 --> 09:04.127
♪ What will be will be ♪

09:06.255 --> 09:09.258
♪ Que sera sera ♪

09:34.283 --> 09:35.575
Fuck!

09:36.743 --> 09:37.619
Fuck.

09:39.496 --> 09:40.831
- Jade.
- What?

09:40.914 --> 09:42.207
Tell me you got something.

09:42.291 --> 09:44.501
Oh, does it fucking look
like I have something?

09:44.584 --> 09:45.961
I...

09:46.044 --> 09:47.462
Okay.

09:49.172 --> 09:50.841
It's all--It's in here.

09:50.924 --> 09:53.427
It's in here. I know it is.

09:53.510 --> 09:55.637
There is-- there is more to what
we need to know and I just--

09:55.721 --> 09:58.098
I can't...Fuck it.

09:59.599 --> 10:01.184
You don't have any acid, do you?

10:01.268 --> 10:02.185
What?

10:02.269 --> 10:04.730
LSD. W-- Listen.

10:04.813 --> 10:07.983
Henry said Miranda
started seeing this place

10:08.066 --> 10:09.609
after an acid trip they took,

10:09.693 --> 10:11.278
which kinda makes sense, given,

10:11.361 --> 10:13.030
you know,
how the brain stores memory.

10:13.113 --> 10:15.407
If it worked for her, it stands
to reason it could work for me.

10:15.490 --> 10:17.743
Oh, okay, um, uh,
take a breath.

10:17.826 --> 10:19.411
Take a breath.

10:19.494 --> 10:22.247
If you're right, and everything
we need is in your brain,

10:22.331 --> 10:24.708
then the last thing we need
is for you to scramble it.

10:24.791 --> 10:26.626
Just take a little time.

10:26.710 --> 10:28.628
Get back to this
after the funeral.

10:28.712 --> 10:31.506
Okay.
I'm not going to the funeral.

10:33.008 --> 10:35.677
Trust me,
I won't be missed.

10:36.678 --> 10:39.765
Look, the best thing
I can do for Tabitha,

10:39.848 --> 10:42.309
for everybody here,

10:42.392 --> 10:46.021
is just find a way to unlock
whatever's locked in here.

10:46.104 --> 10:48.106
How are you gonna do that?

10:49.191 --> 10:50.817
I don't know.

10:51.693 --> 10:53.195
Hey, Jade.

10:54.696 --> 10:56.406
Be careful.

10:56.490 --> 10:58.867
That message on the barn wall
wasn't fucking around.

10:58.950 --> 11:01.078
Whatever answers you may find,

11:01.161 --> 11:03.538
we have no idea
what they're gonna cost.

11:20.347 --> 11:22.307
Are you okay?

11:22.391 --> 11:24.768
It doesn't fit.

11:24.851 --> 11:27.104
[exhales] Honey, I'm sorry.

11:27.187 --> 11:30.607
It was the only thing
I could find in the shed.

11:30.690 --> 11:32.984
You don't have to wear it
if you don't want to.

11:33.068 --> 11:34.444
Yes, I do.

11:34.528 --> 11:36.279
At Grandpa's funeral,

11:36.363 --> 11:39.282
Dad said a man wears a suit
to show his respect.

11:41.618 --> 11:43.245
You look very handsome.

11:46.456 --> 11:48.041
Let's go.

12:07.352 --> 12:10.397
Days like today...

12:10.480 --> 12:12.023
well, they're not easy.

12:13.775 --> 12:15.819
I'm not going to stand here...

12:15.902 --> 12:17.571
- [cawing]
- ...and try to tell you that--

12:17.654 --> 12:21.700
[cawing]

12:21.783 --> 12:23.368
[crowd chattering]

12:23.452 --> 12:26.246
[crows cawing]

12:26.329 --> 12:30.834
[cawing]

12:30.917 --> 12:33.962
[crows cawing]

12:39.718 --> 12:40.969
[cawing]

12:41.052 --> 12:43.346
- Boyd?
- Just...

12:43.430 --> 12:46.725
[cawing]

12:46.808 --> 12:49.269
[crows cawing]

12:55.942 --> 12:57.360
You need to eat.

12:58.737 --> 13:00.614
I'm not hungry.

13:14.461 --> 13:16.379
Hello.

13:16.463 --> 13:18.089
Hi, Victor.

13:20.217 --> 13:21.426
Uh...

13:21.510 --> 13:23.386
Oh.
[stammers]

13:23.470 --> 13:26.848
When I was a boy,
I drew pictures

13:26.932 --> 13:29.267
so that the pictures
would remember.

13:31.603 --> 13:33.438
This is for you.

13:47.327 --> 13:49.788
That's very sweet, Victor.
Thank you so much.

14:00.048 --> 14:02.133
Can I go to the Colony House
with Victor?

14:02.217 --> 14:03.969
No, not today.

14:04.052 --> 14:05.303
Please.

14:05.387 --> 14:07.764
I don't wanna be here.

14:11.393 --> 14:13.144
Is that okay with you?

14:13.228 --> 14:14.521
Yeah.

14:14.604 --> 14:16.106
Okay.

14:18.316 --> 14:19.651
Be safe, okay?

14:22.862 --> 14:26.408
I'll make sure that nothing
happens to him, I promise.

14:27.826 --> 14:29.077
Okay.

14:34.457 --> 14:37.502
Here, you drink this.

14:37.586 --> 14:40.380
And, uh, Bakta's just whipping
you up something to eat.

14:41.548 --> 14:43.758
Has anything like that
ever happened before?

14:45.385 --> 14:47.596
With the-- the crows?

14:47.679 --> 14:49.931
No.

14:50.015 --> 14:51.891
I mean, everybody sees them
when they see the trees,

14:51.975 --> 14:55.020
but that's, uh-- that's new.

14:55.103 --> 14:57.147
When did it get like this?

14:57.230 --> 14:59.649
What do you mean?

14:59.733 --> 15:03.111
Well, Sara, the girl who helped
me with my glasses, she--

15:03.194 --> 15:06.114
she said that after Sheriff Boyd
found the talismans

15:06.197 --> 15:08.992
that for a long time
people were safe.

15:09.075 --> 15:10.785
When did that change?

15:10.869 --> 15:12.120
It was, um...

15:12.203 --> 15:13.997
I guess it was--

15:14.080 --> 15:17.375
It was around the night
that my dad died.

15:17.459 --> 15:20.670
We had lost a family
the night before, the Pratts,

15:20.754 --> 15:22.547
and then Jim and Tabitha,
the Matthews family,

15:22.631 --> 15:25.091
they showed up with Jade.

15:25.175 --> 15:26.843
They came all together?

15:26.926 --> 15:29.471
Um, not in the same car,

15:29.554 --> 15:31.556
just they got here
at the same time.

15:31.640 --> 15:36.311
And ever since then,
things have been bad?

15:37.771 --> 15:39.314
No, no,
that's not what I mean.

15:39.397 --> 15:40.940
Hey, Kenny.

15:41.024 --> 15:42.984
You mind if I borrow him
for a second?

15:43.068 --> 15:44.569
- Come here a second.
- I'll come back.

15:49.574 --> 15:51.201
Hey.

15:51.284 --> 15:53.036
Uh, Sophia, right?

15:55.455 --> 15:56.790
I'm Julie.

15:56.873 --> 15:58.208
I know.

15:58.291 --> 16:00.627
I just wanted to tell you
I'm really sorry

16:00.710 --> 16:02.921
about what happened
to your dad.

16:07.258 --> 16:08.426
How's she doing?

16:12.097 --> 16:14.891
Honestly, I don't--
I don't really know.

16:14.974 --> 16:16.393
I mean, she prays a lot.

16:16.476 --> 16:17.894
Are you fucking kidding me?

16:17.977 --> 16:20.689
I-I didn't mean to upset you.
I-- I'm sorry.

16:20.772 --> 16:22.357
What the fuck
did you mean to do, then?

16:22.440 --> 16:24.693
- Julie...
- No. She thinks it's our fault!

16:24.776 --> 16:26.903
Hey, okay. Everybody,
let's take a breath.

16:26.986 --> 16:28.655
Did you tell her that
all of the bad things

16:28.738 --> 16:30.073
started happening
because we came here?

16:30.156 --> 16:31.574
No, no, that's--

16:31.658 --> 16:33.410
no, I didn't s--
no, that's not what I meant.

16:34.536 --> 16:35.537
Let's go home.

16:35.620 --> 16:36.830
No, fuck this.

16:36.913 --> 16:38.748
This is not our home.

16:38.832 --> 16:40.750
I...[gasps]

16:45.046 --> 16:46.631
Julie.

16:46.715 --> 16:48.508
Julie, stop!

16:49.926 --> 16:51.052
Do you think it's true?

16:51.136 --> 16:53.805
- What?
- That when we got here

16:53.888 --> 16:55.515
that all the bad things that
have happened since we got here,

16:55.598 --> 16:56.766
do you think it's our fault?

16:56.850 --> 16:59.436
No, honey, of course not.

17:00.645 --> 17:02.981
Why did it feel like
those crows were celebrating?

17:05.400 --> 17:09.863
[speaking indistinctly]

17:09.946 --> 17:12.198
[speaking indistinctly]

17:15.493 --> 17:16.828
Sophia.

17:16.911 --> 17:18.538
I'm sorry. I didn't...

17:18.621 --> 17:21.875
It's okay.
Uh, we need to talk. Okay?

17:21.958 --> 17:22.959
Okay.

17:23.042 --> 17:25.211
Poor Julie.

17:26.296 --> 17:27.756
Yeah.

17:27.839 --> 17:29.466
I mean,
it seems like a lifetime ago

17:29.549 --> 17:31.509
when we made that little space
for her in our room.

17:34.888 --> 17:36.306
Yeah.

17:37.390 --> 17:38.475
Hey.

17:42.312 --> 17:46.900
You know, you haven't really
talked much about what happened?

17:48.818 --> 17:51.529
- I'm trying to be okay.
- Yeah.

17:51.613 --> 17:53.990
I am. I'm just...

17:54.073 --> 17:57.118
I'm trying to let go of this.
I just don't know how.

18:00.914 --> 18:02.332
You know what?

18:02.415 --> 18:03.833
I have an idea.
Stay right there.

18:03.917 --> 18:05.502
I'm gonna--
I gotta grab a few things.

18:05.585 --> 18:06.711
Where are you going?

18:06.795 --> 18:07.796
Stay right there.
I'll be right back.

18:11.966 --> 18:15.136
[pensive music plays]

18:27.148 --> 18:31.194
Oh, look. Ethan,
my dad is my roommate now.

18:31.277 --> 18:34.405
This is--
This is his bed right here.

18:34.489 --> 18:36.866
Yeah, it's a good thing

18:36.950 --> 18:38.660
that I threw all my stuff
out the window

18:38.743 --> 18:40.286
because then
it made all this space.

18:43.581 --> 18:48.169
It's nice having
a roommate now, too, be--

18:48.253 --> 18:50.338
because you have
someone to talk to,

18:50.421 --> 18:52.882
you know,
if you're afraid.

18:52.966 --> 18:56.469
[inhaling, exhaling sharply]
And you can talk to me,

18:56.553 --> 18:59.389
you know, if you're ever--
if you're ever afraid.

19:03.685 --> 19:05.270
Are there any lakes here?

19:05.353 --> 19:06.729
What?

19:06.813 --> 19:08.189
Lakes?

19:08.273 --> 19:10.692
Have you seen
any lakes here?

19:10.775 --> 19:14.195
Uh, there's the--
there's the Brundles.

19:14.279 --> 19:16.739
That's not very far from here.

19:16.823 --> 19:18.741
- Can we go see it?
- [Victor] What?

19:18.825 --> 19:21.661
No, I don't like it there.

19:21.744 --> 19:23.162
Water's creepy.

19:23.246 --> 19:25.248
Please.

19:25.331 --> 19:28.042
Why do you wanna
go see the Brundles?

19:28.126 --> 19:31.921
Never mind.
I'll find it myself.

19:32.005 --> 19:34.424
No, but you're supposed
to stay here with me. That...

19:34.507 --> 19:35.884
I don't care.

19:35.967 --> 19:37.427
Well, I do.

19:37.510 --> 19:40.471
- I just need to see the lake.
- Why?

19:40.555 --> 19:44.100
Friends aren't supposed
to keep secrets, Ethan.

19:44.183 --> 19:46.394
[exhaling] Fine.

19:46.477 --> 19:49.022
If you take me to the lake,
I'll tell you.

19:49.105 --> 19:50.857
[groans]

20:23.890 --> 20:28.019
[suspenseful music playing]

20:35.401 --> 20:36.486
[drawer shuts]

21:00.134 --> 21:01.010
[gasps]

21:02.136 --> 21:04.097
What are you doing out here?

21:04.180 --> 21:05.848
I saw you walk off alone.

21:05.932 --> 21:07.725
Thought you might be
doing something stupid,

21:07.809 --> 21:09.435
like going back to the ruins.

21:12.355 --> 21:13.773
Go away.

21:15.274 --> 21:16.484
Julie.

21:16.567 --> 21:19.112
I'm not going
to the ruins, okay?

21:19.195 --> 21:21.656
I need to get something
from our house.

21:21.739 --> 21:23.533
Okay.

21:23.616 --> 21:25.284
Our old house.

21:25.368 --> 21:28.538
Wait, wait.
The one that collapsed?

21:28.621 --> 21:30.123
No. No fuckin' way.

21:30.206 --> 21:32.291
I was inside that thing
when it came down, remember?

21:32.375 --> 21:33.876
- Okay.
- It's just too unstable.

21:33.960 --> 21:35.461
Okay.

21:35.545 --> 21:36.713
No, look, look.

21:36.796 --> 21:39.549
All right, stop, stop. Stop.

21:39.632 --> 21:42.802
What's in there
that's so important?

21:42.885 --> 21:44.637
I told you
that thing that I can do?

21:44.721 --> 21:46.514
My brother called it
Storywalking?

21:46.597 --> 21:48.224
He learned about it
from one of his books,

21:48.307 --> 21:50.268
and all his books
are under the house now,

21:50.351 --> 21:52.520
and I-I need to know if
there's anything in there

21:52.603 --> 21:54.230
about how to control it,
so I can go back

21:54.313 --> 21:55.898
and save my dad
without getting killed.

21:55.982 --> 21:57.400
And maybe
that is stupid, okay?

21:57.483 --> 22:00.903
But I'm not asking
your permission. I'm going.

22:00.987 --> 22:03.656
So you can help me
or you can leave me alone.

22:09.704 --> 22:11.205
Give me that.

22:31.601 --> 22:32.810
You still want that bullet?

22:35.354 --> 22:37.440
There's something
I need you to do for me first.

22:40.109 --> 22:42.487
[Ethan] What's he doing?

22:42.570 --> 22:44.280
[Victor] I think he's sleeping.

22:45.907 --> 22:46.824
Jade?

22:47.992 --> 22:49.911
What?

22:49.994 --> 22:51.621
Let's go.

22:51.704 --> 22:54.415
We just got here.

22:54.499 --> 22:56.125
It's not what I'm looking for.

22:56.209 --> 22:58.002
How do you know that?

22:58.086 --> 22:59.587
I just do.

23:00.922 --> 23:05.134
Ethan, you-- you promised

23:05.218 --> 23:08.137
that if I brought you here,
you would tell me.

23:08.221 --> 23:11.265
I need to find
the Lake of Tears.

23:11.349 --> 23:13.518
It's a lake with magical powers.

23:13.601 --> 23:15.353
What kind of magical powers?

23:15.436 --> 23:17.480
It can make people better
when they're hurt.

23:17.563 --> 23:23.111
I thought I made it up,
but my dad told me it's here.

23:24.362 --> 23:26.405
I need to find it.

23:26.489 --> 23:28.282
When did he tell you that?

23:29.784 --> 23:33.037
Yesterday. Out by the RV?

23:33.121 --> 23:36.541
Maybe once I find it,
it can make him better.

23:36.624 --> 23:38.918
Maybe he'll come back.

23:39.001 --> 23:40.753
Maybe Jade can help.

23:40.837 --> 23:42.630
Jade!

23:42.713 --> 23:44.757
Oh, for Christ's sakes, what?

23:44.841 --> 23:47.051
We need to find
the Lake of Tears!

23:47.135 --> 23:49.428
The lake of what?

23:49.512 --> 23:52.265
It's a kids'
book though, right?

23:52.348 --> 23:55.393
It's stories
made up for little kids?

23:55.476 --> 23:59.522
Before we got here, I thought
monsters were made up, too.

23:59.605 --> 24:00.940
Fair point.

24:07.738 --> 24:09.448
You good?

24:09.532 --> 24:13.244
This is where I talked to my dad
the day the house collapsed.

24:18.082 --> 24:20.668
He was still down there
when the sun was setting.

24:22.837 --> 24:24.797
I was so scared that
we were just gonna lose him

24:24.881 --> 24:26.591
right then and there.

24:29.427 --> 24:30.803
He...

24:33.389 --> 24:37.476
He kept telling me
everything was gonna be okay,

24:37.560 --> 24:39.854
that I shouldn't be afraid.

24:39.937 --> 24:44.567
Hey, uh,
why don't you let me do this?

24:44.650 --> 24:46.027
What?

24:46.110 --> 24:48.738
I can handle a couple of books.

24:48.821 --> 24:50.907
Besides, someone's
gonna need to be up here

24:50.990 --> 24:52.658
if something happens, right?

24:54.869 --> 24:57.163
No, no, I should be the-- it's
my thing. I should be the one--

24:57.246 --> 24:58.873
Hey, hey, hey, hey.

24:58.956 --> 25:02.793
Storywalker,
why don't you let someone else

25:02.877 --> 25:04.712
do the cool shit
for a change, huh?

25:05.922 --> 25:07.798
It's good for my self-esteem.

25:14.639 --> 25:16.682
There's a--
There's a way in over here.

25:22.355 --> 25:23.814
In-- In the story,

25:23.898 --> 25:25.942
Achan caused the whole nation
of Israel to suffer

25:26.025 --> 25:27.610
because he offended God.

25:27.693 --> 25:28.945
And that's
what you told Julie?

25:29.028 --> 25:30.488
I just thought
that maybe, somehow,

25:30.571 --> 25:32.573
they brought some sort of
ill tidings with them--

25:32.657 --> 25:33.574
Okay, stop.

25:33.658 --> 25:35.910
The people here,

25:35.993 --> 25:39.163
they're always one bad day away
from giving up,

25:39.247 --> 25:41.707
giving up, losing hope.

25:41.791 --> 25:45.294
I-I know,
it was-- it was...

25:45.378 --> 25:46.754
I know.

25:49.882 --> 25:51.175
Look...

25:54.512 --> 25:57.723
we need to figure out where
you're gonna live from now on.

25:57.807 --> 26:00.059
Where do you live?

26:00.142 --> 26:04.522
That, uh-- that big house
up on the hill, Colony House.

26:04.605 --> 26:06.983
There's plenty of room there.

26:07.066 --> 26:09.610
But there's-- there's
so many people there.

26:09.694 --> 26:10.736
Yeah.

26:10.820 --> 26:12.780
Can't I just stay
at the clinic?

26:12.863 --> 26:16.909
Well, there's no extra rooms
in the clinic, so...

26:18.119 --> 26:19.912
Where does Sara live?

26:19.996 --> 26:21.372
What?

26:21.455 --> 26:23.833
She was really nice to me.

26:23.916 --> 26:26.544
That's not a good idea.

26:26.627 --> 26:30.464
Because of-- of what she did?

26:33.759 --> 26:36.262
How did you, um...

26:36.345 --> 26:38.431
I've--
I've heard people talking.

26:39.724 --> 26:42.560
Why-- Why would you-- why would
you want to live with her?

26:42.643 --> 26:45.604
Because I've--
Because I've seen her kindness,

26:45.688 --> 26:48.524
and I don't-- I don't think
she's a bad person.

26:52.820 --> 26:55.406
You have no idea
the kind of person she is.

26:59.368 --> 27:02.246
[wood creaking softly]

27:04.623 --> 27:08.169
[Julie] I can't see you at all.
Are you okay?

27:08.252 --> 27:09.712
I'm fine.

27:09.795 --> 27:11.839
Just letting my eyes adjust,
that's all.

27:14.091 --> 27:16.635
How many of these books
am I looking for anyway?

27:16.719 --> 27:19.055
He kept them all
in a little blue bag.

27:19.138 --> 27:20.723
They should be together.

27:20.806 --> 27:23.059
Little blue bag, huh?

27:23.142 --> 27:24.560
Piece of cake.

27:24.643 --> 27:26.979
[wood creaking softly]

27:30.024 --> 27:32.777
[metal creaking]

27:39.367 --> 27:41.118
[wood creaking softly]

27:50.002 --> 27:51.462
Randall?

27:52.588 --> 27:54.632
I'm fine.

27:59.428 --> 28:02.098
What are we doing here?

28:02.181 --> 28:03.766
[exhales]

28:03.849 --> 28:06.894
We got storage sheds
around town.

28:06.977 --> 28:09.063
The storage room in the diner,

28:09.146 --> 28:11.690
they're filled
with clothes, tools,

28:11.774 --> 28:14.110
everything we thought
would be useful.

28:14.193 --> 28:17.113
This is everything else.

28:18.406 --> 28:19.949
Okay.

28:20.032 --> 28:22.243
I want you to treat this place
like a crime scene.

28:22.326 --> 28:27.748
Like, these--these things,
they tell a story, right?

28:27.832 --> 28:29.583
I want you
to develop a narrative.

28:29.667 --> 28:31.210
Tell me everything
there is to know

28:31.293 --> 28:33.254
about the people
this stuff belonged to.

28:33.337 --> 28:34.505
Why?

28:36.632 --> 28:38.134
Because I asked you to.

28:38.217 --> 28:39.593
So, why don't you do it?

28:39.677 --> 28:42.179
You're a cop.
You were trained to do this.

28:42.263 --> 28:44.265
- I wasn't.
- [Acosta] Hm.

28:44.348 --> 28:46.809
There-- There might be things
we overlooked,

28:46.892 --> 28:49.103
something that'll
help us get out of here.

28:49.186 --> 28:51.397
Tell me why we're really here.

28:51.480 --> 28:52.731
- I just did.
- Bullshit.

28:52.815 --> 28:54.191
Hey.

28:54.275 --> 28:56.318
You better tell me
why we're really here.

29:02.366 --> 29:05.870
Because you
remind me of someone.

29:05.953 --> 29:08.289
All right?

29:08.372 --> 29:10.624
You remind me...

29:10.708 --> 29:14.587
of someone I could've
helped and I didn't.

29:17.131 --> 29:19.884
I don't get to get that back.

29:19.967 --> 29:23.345
But I'm gonna stand here and--

29:23.429 --> 29:26.807
Look, I know you think
everything I said is bullshit,

29:26.891 --> 29:28.392
and maybe it is.

29:28.476 --> 29:30.311
Maybe it isn't, all right?

29:30.394 --> 29:32.980
But if you do this for me,

29:33.063 --> 29:35.065
think about all the people
you might be helping,

29:35.149 --> 29:36.734
the people you might be saving.

29:36.817 --> 29:40.321
You think about the cop
who first put that badge on.

29:40.404 --> 29:42.740
You do all that, and you
still want that bullet...

29:44.033 --> 29:46.368
then, yeah, we'll talk.

29:46.452 --> 29:48.370
That's a promise.

30:03.802 --> 30:05.471
[knocking]

30:11.393 --> 30:12.686
Donna?

30:31.080 --> 30:35.167
[pensive music playing]

30:38.379 --> 30:40.923
I think she went back to town.

30:41.006 --> 30:42.091
Oh.

30:42.174 --> 30:43.926
You need something?

30:45.261 --> 30:47.596
Uh, no. I'm-- I'm okay.

30:47.680 --> 30:49.807
Are you?

30:49.890 --> 30:53.852
Forty years, I sat in my house
after my family disappeared.

30:53.936 --> 30:56.522
I was... a lot of things.

30:56.605 --> 30:59.066
"Okay" was never one of them.

31:00.234 --> 31:01.610
I should go home.

31:01.694 --> 31:03.112
Where you headed?

31:03.195 --> 31:05.656
Um, just going home.

31:05.739 --> 31:07.825
Oh. Well, I'll walk with you.

31:07.908 --> 31:10.494
Henry, no, it's okay.
I can go by myself.

31:10.578 --> 31:13.914
Tabitha, I don't think you
should be alone right now.

31:16.458 --> 31:19.461
So, where are
you really going?

31:19.545 --> 31:21.005
I'm going home.

31:21.088 --> 31:23.173
And where are you
going after that?

31:23.257 --> 31:25.676
Henry, I don't know
what you're talking about.

31:25.759 --> 31:28.554
Sure you do. You're good
at a lot of things, Tabitha.

31:28.637 --> 31:30.389
Lying is definitely
not among them.

31:30.472 --> 31:32.099
So we can play
the whole charade

31:32.182 --> 31:33.809
of me dropping
you off at your house

31:33.892 --> 31:36.186
and then waiting to see where
else you go or you can just--

31:36.270 --> 31:39.189
Okay, I'm gonna
find the lighthouse, okay?

31:40.190 --> 31:42.401
I'm gonna find my way
back to the lighthouse.

31:42.484 --> 31:44.486
I got out of here once.

31:44.570 --> 31:49.158
If I find the lighthouse,
I can maybe, maybe, hopefully,

31:49.241 --> 31:51.243
I can do it again and
take my children with me.

31:51.327 --> 31:53.746
I'm not gonna
let them die here.

31:53.829 --> 31:55.998
How? Donna said no one knows
where the lighthouse is...

31:56.081 --> 31:58.083
No, they don't. That's why
I have to do it again,

31:58.167 --> 31:59.335
like I did the last time.

31:59.418 --> 32:01.211
I have to go through
the bottle tree.

32:01.295 --> 32:04.173
The man
in the pool, Dale, right?

32:04.256 --> 32:06.175
He died when
he tried going through.

32:06.258 --> 32:08.427
Yeah, but...
Okay, what if it was...

32:08.510 --> 32:10.346
What if it was
not meant for him?

32:10.429 --> 32:11.889
What if it was
only meant for me?

32:11.972 --> 32:13.432
And what if you're wrong?

32:13.515 --> 32:16.101
What if you end up stuck
in the side of god-knows-what

32:16.185 --> 32:17.645
somewhere no one can--

32:17.728 --> 32:20.105
I don't know. I don't know,
Henry. I have to try.

32:20.189 --> 32:23.859
- Okay. I'm coming with you.
- No, Henry--

32:23.942 --> 32:25.903
You said you're going to
the bottle tree, right?

32:25.986 --> 32:27.821
I wanna see it.
I want to see the tree

32:27.905 --> 32:29.907
my wife died trying to reach.

32:31.116 --> 32:34.036
[sighs]

32:34.119 --> 32:35.788
Henry, I have
to tell you something--

32:35.871 --> 32:39.333
She was my wife. Please.

32:42.544 --> 32:44.880
Okay. Let's go.

32:44.963 --> 32:46.173
- Okay.
- Yeah.

32:51.970 --> 32:53.055
Where are we going?

32:53.138 --> 32:55.265
It's just a little further.

32:57.643 --> 33:00.104
Why won't you tell me
what's in the bag?

33:00.187 --> 33:01.522
You'll see.

33:10.531 --> 33:12.116
Ever heard of a rage room?

33:12.199 --> 33:15.327
They're really popular in Japan.

33:15.411 --> 33:20.249
It's sort of a way to
lash out, you know, let go

33:20.332 --> 33:23.085
without hurting somebody
or breaking shit that you need.

33:29.925 --> 33:31.427
Ellis, this is really sweet,

33:31.510 --> 33:33.595
but I don't know
how this is gonna help--

33:33.679 --> 33:35.848
When my mom died,

33:35.931 --> 33:37.808
you were the one
that brought me back.

33:39.435 --> 33:42.187
You didn't even
know me very well,

33:42.271 --> 33:45.441
but you knew that
I was still in there,

33:45.524 --> 33:47.735
underneath all the...

33:47.818 --> 33:50.863
the dark, horrible shit
that I was going through,

33:50.946 --> 33:53.282
and you never gave up on me,

33:53.365 --> 33:55.993
not until you finally
pulled me out.

33:56.076 --> 33:58.412
It's my turn now.

33:58.495 --> 33:59.788
Give it a shot.

34:02.374 --> 34:03.500
So...

34:04.710 --> 34:06.628
you want the crowbar...

34:08.547 --> 34:10.257
or the bat?

34:21.268 --> 34:23.270
Definitely the bat.

34:23.353 --> 34:25.773
That's my girl.

34:25.856 --> 34:27.524
[exhales heavily]

34:35.783 --> 34:36.992
[thuds]

34:37.075 --> 34:39.119
[laughs]

34:39.203 --> 34:40.454
[laughs]

34:41.705 --> 34:43.332
It's all yours.

35:06.563 --> 35:08.690
[cries out]

35:08.774 --> 35:10.317
[screaming]

35:14.071 --> 35:16.907
Okay, so, let me
get this straight.

35:16.990 --> 35:20.410
You made up this Lake of Tears

35:20.494 --> 35:25.207
as part of a game that you used
to play with finger puppets.

35:25.290 --> 35:28.544
It wasn't a game.
It was a story.

35:28.627 --> 35:31.046
Okay, so, you told
a story about this lake

35:31.129 --> 35:34.091
and some finger puppets,
and now-- now what?

35:34.174 --> 35:35.592
You think the lake is here

35:35.676 --> 35:40.138
because your dad told you
that you need to find it?

35:40.222 --> 35:42.891
Maybe I didn't make it up.

35:42.975 --> 35:44.643
Maybe I just thought I did.

35:47.479 --> 35:49.523
I'm confused.

35:49.606 --> 35:52.109
Do you remember the red rocks
we found at the settlement?

35:52.192 --> 35:53.318
Oh, yeah.

35:53.402 --> 35:54.903
My mom thought
she made them up

35:54.987 --> 35:56.905
because she used to have
nightmares about them.

35:56.989 --> 35:59.491
But the reason
she saw those rocks

35:59.575 --> 36:01.535
was because they were here.

36:01.618 --> 36:04.955
Maybe it's the same
with the lake.

36:05.038 --> 36:08.709
Maybe I used it in my story

36:08.792 --> 36:12.212
because it's real,
and I just didn't know.

36:14.756 --> 36:16.550
What were you doing
at the Brundles?

36:16.633 --> 36:19.720
It's an old
meditation technique.

36:19.803 --> 36:21.555
[Ethan]
Why were you meditating?

36:21.638 --> 36:24.766
[Jade] Because I...
[exhaling sharply]

36:24.850 --> 36:26.935
I'm trying to
remember something.

36:27.019 --> 36:30.898
I'm trying to remember
something that I used to know,

36:30.981 --> 36:33.692
something that'll
help us leave.

36:34.735 --> 36:36.653
[Ethan] So, we're both
looking for something

36:36.737 --> 36:38.864
that can help everyone.

36:38.947 --> 36:42.034
[Jade] I guess we are.

36:42.117 --> 36:43.785
Hey, Victor,
we got a lake to find.

36:49.374 --> 36:51.585
Victor?

36:51.668 --> 36:53.170
Hey.

36:57.424 --> 36:59.259
What is that?

36:59.343 --> 37:00.761
[urine dripping]

37:02.846 --> 37:04.806
Victor.

37:04.890 --> 37:07.309
[crow cawing]

37:07.392 --> 37:09.686
[cawing]

37:09.770 --> 37:12.147
- [crows cawing]
- [Ethan] Victor!

37:12.230 --> 37:13.482
Victor! Come on.

37:13.565 --> 37:15.067
[cawing]

37:15.150 --> 37:16.568
- Victor!
- [Ethan] Victor!

37:16.652 --> 37:17.569
[cawing]

37:19.780 --> 37:22.074
[wood creaking softly]

37:23.283 --> 37:25.243
[Randall] Jesus!

37:25.327 --> 37:26.578
Fuck!

37:26.662 --> 37:27.704
What?

37:27.788 --> 37:30.207
Ah. Nothing. I'm good.

37:31.917 --> 37:33.543
Ah, fuck.

37:36.254 --> 37:37.881
I see the bag.

37:40.092 --> 37:41.635
[clattering]

37:41.718 --> 37:42.594
[creaking]

37:43.762 --> 37:45.138
[knocking]

37:51.228 --> 37:52.187
Kenny.

37:53.647 --> 37:55.148
Is everything all right?

37:55.232 --> 37:57.651
[Kenny] Sophia and I
have been talking

37:57.734 --> 38:01.822
about where she wants
to live from now on.

38:01.905 --> 38:03.407
Okay.

38:03.490 --> 38:07.035
And if it's all right,
she would like to live here,

38:07.119 --> 38:08.787
with you.

38:10.789 --> 38:11.707
Oh.

38:15.836 --> 38:17.546
Okay. Sure.

38:17.629 --> 38:18.922
[Kenny]
Okay.

38:19.006 --> 38:21.174
Okay. Come on.

38:21.258 --> 38:23.010
Let's go.

38:24.136 --> 38:25.721
Randall?

38:25.804 --> 38:28.598
Randall?
What's going on?

38:28.682 --> 38:30.809
Ah, just gimme a sec.

38:36.857 --> 38:38.442
I got the bag.

38:38.525 --> 38:39.985
What are the titles?

38:40.068 --> 38:43.071
Uh...

38:43.155 --> 38:46.658
Grand Gooligog.
The Cromenockle.

38:46.742 --> 38:48.785
Okay, that's them!
Get out of there!

38:48.869 --> 38:50.579
Yeah. All right.

38:53.331 --> 38:54.458
All right.

38:57.586 --> 38:59.629
It's just you and me, pal.

38:59.713 --> 39:01.548
[wood creaking softly]

39:01.631 --> 39:03.216
Ah, fuck.

39:07.345 --> 39:08.305
[screeching]

39:10.348 --> 39:11.725
[squeaking]

39:12.851 --> 39:15.187
[Julie]
Randall?

39:16.354 --> 39:17.397
Randall?

39:17.481 --> 39:19.357
Ah, I'm okay.

39:19.441 --> 39:21.276
Yeah, I'm okay.

39:23.945 --> 39:26.573
Better?

39:26.656 --> 39:29.201
A little, yeah.

39:29.284 --> 39:31.078
Well, it's a start, right?

39:31.161 --> 39:32.245
Yeah.

39:41.296 --> 39:44.925
I'm gonna, uh...
I'm gonna go take a nap.

39:45.008 --> 39:46.635
Yeah, I told Donna
that I was gonna start

39:46.718 --> 39:48.678
getting things ready
for the food run tomorrow.

39:48.762 --> 39:49.679
Okay?

39:49.763 --> 39:50.764
Okay.

39:53.892 --> 39:55.811
And, hey, um...

39:55.894 --> 39:58.188
thank you for today.

40:00.232 --> 40:02.025
You're welcome.

40:04.486 --> 40:07.030
[pensive music playing]

40:18.792 --> 40:20.502
[knocking]

40:20.585 --> 40:21.545
It's me.

40:26.967 --> 40:30.345
I did the best I could.
Think it's gonna be enough?

40:30.428 --> 40:32.222
It's a great start.

40:32.305 --> 40:35.225
But I think we're gonna
need a little bit more.

40:40.689 --> 40:42.190
Oh.

40:42.274 --> 40:45.068
Yeah, Victor told me this
is where Miranda was going

40:45.152 --> 40:48.488
when... when she died.

40:50.031 --> 40:52.868
He took me
to her grave, but I...

40:52.951 --> 40:55.412
I don't think he could bear
to take me here.

40:58.331 --> 41:02.961
This looks just like
the one she made back home.

41:05.088 --> 41:07.716
Except for this.

41:18.810 --> 41:20.437
Go back to town, Henry.

41:20.520 --> 41:22.439
- Tabitha, you can't do this.
- Henry, please, I...

41:22.522 --> 41:23.982
Look, I was hoping
you'd realize it

41:24.065 --> 41:25.525
on your own
by the time we got here.

41:25.609 --> 41:27.235
Henry, I told you,
the tree is the one--

41:27.319 --> 41:29.321
Yes, the tree is
meant only for you.

41:29.404 --> 41:32.574
And-- And-- And what if it
isn't? What if you're wrong?

41:32.657 --> 41:35.994
What if you end up stuck
in some wall somewhere,

41:36.077 --> 41:37.829
gasping for air, alone?

41:37.913 --> 41:41.750
What happens to Julie and Ethan?

41:41.833 --> 41:45.170
I left a note for Donna.

41:45.253 --> 41:47.005
She'll make sure
to take care of them.

41:47.088 --> 41:49.299
- [Henry] You left a note?
- Yes, I did.

41:49.382 --> 41:52.844
Boy, well, I didn't realize
you'd left a note.

41:52.928 --> 41:55.180
I'm sure they'll be just fine.

41:56.806 --> 42:00.810
Am I supposed to do nothing?

42:00.894 --> 42:03.688
Finding the lighthouse could be
what gets everyone home.

42:03.772 --> 42:04.981
- And if it's not?
- I don't know!

42:05.065 --> 42:07.025
- I'll try something else!
- Not if you're dead!

42:07.108 --> 42:09.236
Then what the fuck am I supposed
to do, Henry? Move!

42:09.319 --> 42:10.862
- I don't know!
- Will you move, please?

42:10.946 --> 42:13.698
I don't know!
I wish I did know.

42:13.782 --> 42:15.450
But if you wanna go
through this tree...

42:17.160 --> 42:19.120
you're gonna have
to go through me first.

42:19.204 --> 42:21.498
Henry, move.

42:21.581 --> 42:22.624
Please, Henry.

42:22.707 --> 42:25.293
Your kids need you.

42:25.377 --> 42:27.254
Ethan and Julie.

42:28.630 --> 42:30.632
Tabitha?

42:40.267 --> 42:41.518
Why are you here?

42:42.936 --> 42:44.771
Why do you look so different?

42:44.854 --> 42:47.148
Those are
the wrong questions.

42:49.609 --> 42:53.405
Will that tree take me
back to the lighthouse?

42:53.488 --> 42:55.323
- I don't think so.
- [Tabitha] Wait.

42:55.407 --> 42:57.242
You don't think so?

42:57.325 --> 42:59.077
You told me
it was the only way.

42:59.160 --> 43:01.746
It was, but that was before.

43:01.830 --> 43:03.081
[Tabitha]
Yeah, but before--

43:03.164 --> 43:05.458
Okay, you need to stop
talking in riddles.

43:05.542 --> 43:07.127
You're getting so close now,

43:07.210 --> 43:09.212
but I'm afraid
you're running out of time.

43:10.505 --> 43:11.756
[Ethan]
Victor!

43:15.802 --> 43:16.928
- Victor!
- Okay.

43:17.012 --> 43:18.430
It came from over there.
Come on.

43:21.516 --> 43:22.559
Victor.

43:23.977 --> 43:25.228
What happened?

43:25.312 --> 43:26.813
[Tabitha]
Ethan?

43:26.896 --> 43:27.981
We're over here!

43:28.064 --> 43:29.691
Ethan!

43:30.817 --> 43:31.818
Oh, honey.

43:31.901 --> 43:34.571
[whimpering]

43:34.654 --> 43:36.031
Hey, Victor.

43:36.114 --> 43:39.117
Hey. Hey, talk to me, son.

43:40.744 --> 43:43.621
I told-- I-I told myself
that it wasn't real.

43:43.705 --> 43:45.290
I told myself it wasn't real.

43:45.373 --> 43:46.374
Shh.

43:46.458 --> 43:48.793
It's okay, buddy.

43:48.877 --> 43:52.547
It's okay.
You're all right, Son.

43:52.630 --> 43:54.466
It's okay, Son. It's okay.

43:54.549 --> 43:56.551
It's all right.
You're all right.

43:56.634 --> 43:59.054
It's all right. Hey, hey.

44:13.443 --> 44:14.986
I'll be damned.

44:24.954 --> 44:26.790
Hey, Abbs.

44:32.462 --> 44:34.381
Been a while.

44:38.885 --> 44:40.595
Things are, uh...

44:43.890 --> 44:45.475
Yeah, things are changing.

44:48.395 --> 44:50.522
I am changing.

44:53.566 --> 44:58.238
Done some things recently
and said some things...

45:03.952 --> 45:06.079
I don't know
if I like who I'm becoming.

45:09.833 --> 45:12.127
But I don't know who else to be.

45:15.296 --> 45:17.674
Tabitha and-- and Jade,

45:17.757 --> 45:21.010
uh, if what they're saying,

45:21.094 --> 45:22.887
what they remember,

45:22.971 --> 45:27.058
if it's true, it feels like,
for the first time,

45:27.142 --> 45:28.810
we're close to something.

45:30.228 --> 45:32.856
Yeah, but none
of it matters if...

45:32.939 --> 45:35.316
if I can't hold
these people together.

45:38.153 --> 45:39.988
If I lose these people
right now, I....

45:41.322 --> 45:43.074
Yeah.

45:45.994 --> 45:48.538
I could really use some help.

45:51.249 --> 45:53.376
I-I-I don't know
if there's anything you can do,

45:53.460 --> 45:58.214
but if you can hear me...

45:58.298 --> 45:59.966
What the...! Hey!

46:00.049 --> 46:01.301
No, no!
[struggling]

46:01.384 --> 46:04.053
No, no, no! Hey! Hey! Hey!

46:04.137 --> 46:07.891
[struggling]

46:12.103 --> 46:14.397
[gasping for breath]

46:14.481 --> 46:19.277
[breathing heavily]

46:22.155 --> 46:23.740
What the...?

46:23.823 --> 46:25.533
What the...?

46:25.617 --> 46:27.577
What the fuck is...?

46:31.956 --> 46:33.791
[theme music plays]
